        "text": "- Home\n- Meet Ann\n- Citywide and District 3 Goals\n- News\n- Get Involved\n  - Make Endorsement\n  - Yard Signs\n  - Volunteer\n- Contribute\n- Voter Information\n# Join Our Campaign\nSign up to receive the latest news and updates.\nFirst name Email Zip/Postal Phone Message\nBy providing your phone number you consent to receive messages. Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Text STOP to opt out.\nThank you for signing up!\n# Why I’m Running\nEvery family in City of Millbrae deserves to know that their concerns are being treated as real priorities — not campaign talking points. Our community is ready for leadership that reflects that. We need serious people on our City Council who have real experience and real commitment to our City. I have that proven record and we have work to do!\nThat’s why I’m running for City Council, District 3. I see what City of Millbrae can be when we put people first, and I’m committed to making that vision a reality.\n# Millbrae District 3 the heart of Millbrae\n## Homes on the edge of the district boundaries but next to the district are in District 3.\nIf you live on the edge and within the rose colored Distrct 3 area then you can vote in the November's Special City Council race to fill the remaining two years of this term. This seat became vacant with Mayor Reuben Holober resigned on May 12, 2026.\n# Millbrae District 3 the heart of Millbrae\n## Homes on the edge of the district boundaries but next to the district are in District 3.\nIf you live on the edge and within the rose colored Distrct 3 area then you can vote in the November's Special City Council race to fill the remaining two years of this term. This seat became vacant with Mayor Reuben Holober resigned on May 12, 2026\nMake a Donation\n$10 $15 $25 $50 $100 $250 $500 $1000 $1500 $5900 Other\n- Voter Information\n- Endorsements\n- Yard Signs\n- Events\n- Photos\n- Contact\nAnn Schneider for Millbrae City Council District 3 2026 FPPC # 1494939\nPowered by CampaignPartner.com\n- Home\n- Meet Ann\n- Citywide and District 3 Goals\n- Endorsements\n- Contribute\n- Volunteer\n- News\n- Yard Signs\n- Events\n- Contact\n- Voter Information\nClose Menu",
